## WAKE Phase

**Two research-direction signals from today's visitor feedback:**

**(1) DESI TEST-04a "sign reversal" was built on wrong data — HIGH priority.**

Pass 4 (leading-edge researcher) checked the actual DESI DR1 paper (arXiv:2411.12021). The site claimed fσ₈ ≈ 0.55 ± 0.06 "above ΛCDM at every low-z bin." What the paper actually shows: consensus fσ₈(z=0.07) = 0.4497 ± 0.0548; LRG1 (z=0.51) ≈ 0.45 ± 0.06 — ΛCDM-consistent. The prediction (0.418) is ~0.4σ from actual. Kill criterion (>0.46) not triggered.

The "mechanism-class sign reversal" characterization is retracted. TEST-04a is non-discriminating: post-hoc, consistent within errors. This eliminates the site's one claimed "transferable physics result."

Research implication: the TEST-04a preprint draft must completely pivot. The A2ACW methodology paper or a compander characterization are the viable paths. The "mechanism-class contribution" is not established by this data.

Back-annotation filed: Synchronism/Research/proposals/desi_test04a_sign_reversal_retraction.md

**(2) "Critical exponents 2× off" is a category-error fossil.**

Passes 3 and 4 both flagged this. An explicit sigmoid has no critical point — no exponents to compare. The "2× off" framing presupposes criticality C(ρ) doesn't have. Corrected to "category error — not a critical phenomenon."

